## Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a “card” (a `<div>` with some content) that rotates 180 deg around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body {
  display:flex;
  justify-content:center;
  align-items:center;
  min-height:100vh;
  margin:0;
  background:#f0f0f0;
  font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card container ---------- */
.card {
  width:260px;
  height:160px;
  perspective:800px;          /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Card inner wrapper (the part that actually rotates) ---------- */
.card-inner {
  width:100%;
  height:100%;
  position:relative;
  transition:transform 0.6s ease;   /* smooth animation */
  transform-style:preserve-3d;      /* keep children in 3D space */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Front & back faces ---------- */
.card-front,
.card-back {
  position:absolute;
  width:100%;
  height:100%;
  backface-visibility:hidden;       /* hide the back face when turned */
  border-radius:12px;
  box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.15);
  display:flex;
  justify-content:center;
  align-items:center;
  font-size:1.2rem;
  color:#fff;
}

/* Front face styling */
.card-front {
  background:#4a90e2;
}

/* Back face styling */
.card-back {
  background:#e94e77;
  transform:rotateY(180deg);        /* start rotated so it's hidden */
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣ Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover .card-inner {
  transform:rotateY(180deg);        /* flip the card on hover */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-inner">
    <div class="card-front">
      Front
    </div>
    <div class="card-back">
      Back
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| **1** | `perspective` on `.card` | Gives the 3D effect; without it the rotation would look flat. |
| **2** | `.card-inner` holds the two faces | We rotate this wrapper, not the faces themselves. |
| **3** | `backface-visibility:hidden` | Hides the back side when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| **4** | `transform:rotateY(180deg)` on `.card-back` | Positions the back face behind the front face initially. |
| **5** | Hover → `transform:rotateY(180deg)` on `.card-inner` | Flips the whole wrapper, revealing the back face. |

Feel free to replace the text, colors, or add more content inside the faces.  
If you want a different axis (e.g., X‑axis) just change `rotateY` to `rotateX`.
